; Cross-plugin runtime staging. Plugin `front` form `seed` lowers via
; test/to-row-v1, which emits a bare `row` form. The only `row` declared
; in the aggregate lives in plugin `back`, so the bare `:produces` head
; and the emitted form both resolve cross-plugin (lookupForm spans every
; loaded plugin). `back/row` requires `:v`, which the hook never supplies
; — so the `missing_required_key` on `[row]` can ONLY appear if the
; emitted form was materialized and validated against plugin `back`'s
; schema. That is the proof a cross-plugin lowering stage executed: the
; producing form and its target live in different plugins, and lowering
; bridges them with no bespoke cross-plugin machinery.
(plugin :name front :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name seed :open true
    :lowering (lowering :hook test/to-row-v1 :produces [row])))

(plugin :name back :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name row
    (key :name v :type number :optional false)))

(seed)
